  v_complete_request["The request does not <br/>complete automatically when <br/>the last buffer completes. <br/>The handler must explicitly <br/>call completeRequest from <br/>the CameraManager thread <br/>and must not access the <br/>request after it returns. <br/>The handler may pass <br/>completed requests without <br/>an ordering constraint, and <br/>they are returned to the <br/>application in submission <br/>order."]
  v_complete["complete asserts that the <br/>request is RequestPending <br/>and has no pending buffers. <br/>It sets the status to <br/>RequestCancelled if <br/>cancelled#95; is true and to <br/>RequestComplete if it is <br/>false. doCancelRequest sets <br/>cancelled#95; to true even <br/>when pending#95; is empty."]
  v_front{"If the queue is not empty, <br/>it checks the front <br/>request. If the front <br/>request is RequestPending, <br/>the loop stops without <br/>notifying it."}
  v_pop["If the front request is no <br/>longer pending, it asserts <br/>that the request has no <br/>pending buffers and removes <br/>it from the queue with <br/>pop#95;front."]
